From 82a671ab88f8d9c823d3262c2d23d2628d913376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:30:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 140/171] cmd/sing-box: the command line in an importable
 package, cli

The commands of sing-box were package main: no other program could run
them. They are now package cli (cmd/sing-box/cli), with Main and
Command; cmd/sing-box keeps a main that calls cli.Main, so the program
is built from the same path as before, and the completions are written
from cli.Command.

A program that embeds sing-box (podkop) runs the same commands under the
name sing-box beside commands of its own.

The client of the API service (cmd_api*.go, gRPC, about 5 MB) is left out
of a build with the tag podkop_slim: a module build cannot remove the
files, as the package of podkop-engine did. A build without the tag
keeps it.
